# SECURITY — XSS, CSP, third-party network
File: website/audit/security.oot

Verdict: FAIL-CLOSED on stored HTML injection in the markdown
path. CSP allows unsafe-inline script. The page loads Google
Fonts and posts email to collect.openooda.org.

## 1. simpleMarkdown preserves raw HTML (Red 4)

src/main.js simpleMarkdown (line 56) copies every HTML tag out
of the pulled JSON, then writes it back after escaping the rest.

  text.replace(/<[a-zA-Z\/][^>]*>/g, function (match) {
    htmlBlocks.push(match);
    ...
  });
  // later
  return htmlBlocks[parseInt(idx, 10)] || "";

contentEl.innerHTML = html follows that parse.
A compromised or mistaken pulled/*.json field becomes script.
data.title and data.source are concatenated without escapeHtml.
Error paths concatenate err.message into innerHTML.

isExternalUrl allows http, https, mailto, irc, ircs, magnet.
It does not allow javascript:. wikiLinks escape the href.
The raw-HTML preserve path bypasses that check.

Fix: delete the RAWHTML preserve. Run escapeHtml on title,
source, and error text. Use textContent for errors.

## 2. Content-Security-Policy

index.html and 404.html set:

  script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'
  style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com
  font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com
  connect-src 'self' https://collect.openooda.org
  form-action https://collect.openooda.org

'unsafe-inline' is required by the theme boot script in <head>.
That script reads a cookie and sets data-theme. Move it to
src/ and drop 'unsafe-inline' from script-src.
Google Fonts is ambient network authority on every page load.
WORKFLOW.oot §0.3 asks for monospace. The CSS already lists
ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas. Delete the
Google Fonts link. Host nothing from fonts.googleapis.com.

## 3. Email collect

The join form POSTs to https://collect.openooda.org/v1/emails.
The host is not this repo. Capability story: the public page
grants the browser NetCap to a third origin by default.
Honeypot field `website` is present. CSRF token is not.
credentials: omit is set. That is the only fail-closed choice
in this path.

If collect.openooda.org is required, document the origin and
the data retained. If it is not required, delete the form.

## 4. 404.json-ld

404.html embeds `<script type="application/ld+json">{}</script>`.
Empty JSON-LD is a lie to crawlers. Delete it or give it a
real SoftwareApplication block that matches index.html.

## 5. install.sh pipe to bash

website/install.sh:

  curl -fsSL "...packaging/main/install.sh" "$@" | bash

Users who hit /install.sh execute remote shell with no
signature check in this file. The canonical script lives in
packaging/. This file adds a second download hop.
Keep the URL. Do not add more shell.

## 6. Reduced motion

initGlobalDogfight registers with respectReducedMotion: false.
styles/main.css hides #sky under prefers-reduced-motion.
The dogfight canvas stays on. That ignores the user signal.

## 7. Next repair (this repo)

1. Kill RAWHTML in simpleMarkdown. Escape all interpolated
   strings.
2. Drop Google Fonts. Drop 'unsafe-inline' after the theme
   boot script moves out of the HTML.
3. Honor prefers-reduced-motion in the dogfight, or delete
   the dogfight (spa-drag.oot).
4. Delete empty JSON-LD on 404.html.
